id: pm-wlxf8f
title: "CLI argv keeps one value silently when two spellings of one extension flag differ (--status-filter a -s b), while direct callers are refused with extension_option_spelling_conflict"
description: "Found by CodeRabbit on PR 1682 (pm-gh1665). The shared extension option normalizer now refuses two spellings of one declared flag with different values for PmClient.run, MCP and the test harness (extension_option_spelling_conflict). CLI argv dispatch still folds them through mergeAliasOptionKeys in src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts: for scalar flags the canonical value wins and the alias value is dropped without a refusal, so pm demo --status-filter open -s closed silently runs with open. The parse-time occurrences recorded by parseLooseCommandOptions carry enough information to apply the same conflict check before dispatch. Changing this alters CLI behavior for existing scripts that repeat a flag under two spellings, so it was deferred from the batch. Duplicate check: searched spelling conflict, alias folding, repeated flag values and short alias across all statuses; pm-kfq5 owns list accumulation across long/short occurrences, not scalar conflicts."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[4]: agent-ux,cli,extensions,flags
created_at: "2026-11-07T13:26:16.419Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T19:16:34.635Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-07T19:07:15.107Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-07T19:07:15.107Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "CLI argv that supplies two spellings of one declared scalar extension flag with different values exits 2 with extension_option_spelling_conflict naming both spellings and the handler key; Equal values and list flags keep their current accumulation; A spec drives the built CLI with --long and -s spellings, with a negative control that restores silent folding"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
repro_steps: "Declare --status-filter with short -s, run pm demo --status-filter open -s closed --json"
resolution: "Each command records the tokens its own option parser receives (captureCommandOptionTokens). refuseConflictingArgvOptionSpellings (src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts) replays Commander's parseOptions rules over every command on the dispatch path: short groups, required/optional/variadic values, negative numbers, --long=value, the positional and pass-through stop rules, registered ownership and negations, plus the loose grammar for unregistered declared flags. It refuses with extension_option_spelling_conflict when two spellings hold different values after coercion. Equal values, repeats of one spelling and list flags are unchanged. Codex review rounds 1-3 hardened the scan."
expected_result: pm demo --status-filter open -s closed exits 2 with extension_option_spelling_conflict naming both spellings
actual_result: "Built-CLI spec refuses separate, attached and grouped spellings, and accepts equal values, list accumulation and repeated-spelling last-wins; real-Commander specs cover ancestor consumption, positional and pass-through stops and core short-alias ownership; negative control without captured tokens keeps the last value silently"
affected_version: 2026.11.7
component: extensions
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
